2.2. Isothermal hot compression experiment 
 
The isothermal hot compression of φ8mm × 12 mm cylinder was carried out by Gleeble-3800 thermal simulation testing machine. The process route is shown in Fig. 1 a. Firstly, the sample was heated to 1250 °C at 10 °C/s and held for 3 min to homogenize the structure. Then it was cooled to the set temperature (950–1250 °C) and held for 30 s, and then the experiment was carried out according to the set compression experimental parameters (strain rate 0.01–50s-1, deformation 60 %). The hot compression specimen was cut off by wire cutting, and the central part was observed ( Fig. 1 c). 
