3.5. Fabrication and performance evaluation 
 
After forging, heating, extrusion, acid pickling, cold drawing, solution annealing, grinding, compaction, and aging, three 200 kg ingots were fabricated into three different specifications pipes ( Fig. 14 a–h). Due to the large deformation with a fast extrusion speed, both the corner and surface regions of the extruded square-in-round pipes obtained a uniform recrystallized microstructure ( Fig. 15 a and c). Owing to the quenching delay of the extruded pipes exceeding 50s, it is believed that the recrystallized grains with low GND (0.8 × 10 14  m −2 observed in Fig. S1 ) are obtained from Post-DRX. After cold drawing and solution heat treatment, the final pipes with homogeneous fine equiaxed grains ( Fig. 15 d and f)) resulting from SRX were obtained. 
